  <div id="part2">
    <h2>2. The Metacircular Silicon Loop &amp; Universal Compiler Soundness</h2>
    <p>How do we guarantee that a functional expression compiled to physical silicon pin transactions computes the <em>exact</em> denotational value — for every possible 64-bit input, without trusting hand-written testbench assertions? In <code>lib/silicon/inet-compiler.hypercubical</code>, we eliminate the gap between compiler, hardware semantics, and testbench with a single-source wire-graph AST:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>One Wire-Graph AST (<code>INetSlot</code>, <code>ic-graph</code>):</strong> Every source expression <code>e : HExpr</code> compiles once into a concrete <code>List INetSlot</code> hardware wire graph — specifying each slot's ID, node kind (<code>ik-num</code>, <code>ik-add</code>, <code>ik-add1</code>, <code>ik-dup</code>, <code>ik-free</code>), principal port <code>p0</code>, auxiliary port <code>p1</code>, and byte value.</li>
      <li><strong>Structural Pin Emitter (<code>compile-hexpr</code>):</strong> <code>compile-hexpr e = list-append ic-clear-all (ic-emit-slots (ic-graph e))</code> folds directly over <code>ic-graph e</code> to emit exact Tiny Tapeout <code>load_field(slot, field, byte)</code> pin transactions for <code>tt_um_hyperinet</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Single-Pass Dual-Lane Semantics (<code>inet-cycle-go</code>, <code>inet-run-cnt</code>):</strong> Structurally recursive on <code>List INetSlot</code> with zero fuel, firing all disjoint active pairs (`p0[a] = 4·b ∧ p0[b] = 4·a`) simultaneously on every clock edge and threading pending <code>rewire(dst, ref)</code> updates forward.</li>
      <li><strong>Proof-Projected Testbench (<code>ic-expect-out</code>, <code>metacircular-tb-sv</code>):</strong> The self-checking SystemVerilog harness projects its readout slots from <code>ic-out-slots e</code> and expected bytes from <code>hexpr-eval-hi e</code> / <code>hexpr-eval-lo e</code> — spec and testbench can never drift apart.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="thm-box">
      <div class="thm-head"><span>Checked Theorems · Universal Metacircular Compiler Soundness</span><span><code>lib/silicon/inet-compiler.hypercubical</code></span></div>
      <div class="eq-box">$$\forall\, e : \mathrm{HExpr},\quad \mathrm{inet\_readout}\; e\; \bigl(\mathrm{fst}\;(\mathrm{inet\_run\_cnt}\; 2\; (\mathrm{ic\_graph}\; e))\bigr) \;\equiv\; (\mathrm{hexpr\_eval\_hi}\; e,\; \mathrm{hexpr\_eval\_lo}\; e)$$</div>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;">Proved universally across all 4 constructors and arbitrary symbolic <code>Word</code> inputs in <strong>4 lines of <code>refl</code></strong> (<code>ic-compile-sound</code>), paired with universal dual-lane 2.0 redexes/cycle parallelism (<code>ic-par-dual-fire-4 : ∀ a b c d, snd (inet-run-cnt 2 (ic-graph (hx-par-add a b c d))) ≡ #4</code>) and the proof-carrying compiler package <code>ic-compile-cert</code>.</p>
    </div>

